{"uid":"9c2ccf8317c15e57","name":"test_the_sandbox_gate_refuses_a_production_alias_by_default","fullName":"tests.test_deployment_environment_policy#test_the_sandbox_gate_refuses_a_production_alias_by_default","historyId":"bb7b25197f33eea4ef5cb075fefec6cc","time":{"start":1793167005794,"stop":1793167005804,"duration":10},"description":"The default is now strict, and this test is the record of that reversal.\n\n    It previously asserted the opposite — \"shipped behaviour must be unchanged:\n    this is hardening, not a migration\" — on the reasoning that MCP can be strict\n    because it is a deliberate integration while registered tools are ubiquitous.\n    That reasoning was about *migration cost*, not about whether the boundary is\n    adequate, and the boundary is not: the built-in sandbox is a process\n    boundary, not a container or seccomp one, so a production alias executing\n    registered tool code had no OS-enforced isolation and nothing said so.\n\n    This is a breaking change, taken deliberately. The escape hatch below is one\n    setting, and unlike the previous default it is visible in the config.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>The default is now strict, and this test is the record of that reversal.</p>\n<pre><code>It previously asserted the opposite — &quot;shipped behaviour must be unchanged:\nthis is hardening, not a migration&quot; — on the reasoning that MCP can be strict\nbecause it is a deliberate integration while registered tools are ubiquitous.\nThat reasoning was about *migration cost*, not about whether the boundary is\nadequate, and the boundary is not: the built-in sandbox is a process\nboundary, not a container or seccomp one, so a production alias executing\nregistered tool code had no OS-enforced isolation and nothing said so.\n\nThis is a breaking change, taken deliberately. The escape hatch below is one\nsetting, and unlike the previous default it is visible in the config.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed"